 images, with each category containing an equal number of images.\n2.\n\n# 4. Detecting Image Attribution in RGB\n\nIn this section, we benchmark image attribution performance across 12 modern text-to-image generators, examining the impact of various architectures, training sizes, and cross-domain influences on task performance. We then analyze the detectability of traces for various hyperparameter adjustments during inference time. Finally, inspired by typical user workflows, we investigate whether AI-generated images can still be attributed to their original generators after being modified by distinct software or models.\n\n## 4.1. Training Image Attributors\n\n**Problem Setup and Model Performance.** Prior research has demonstrated deep networks’ ability to distinguish AI-generated images from real ones [9, 16, 37, 48, 50, 54, 77] and identify their sources [8, 69, 82]. Our study builds on this foundation by merging the tasks of discerning “AI-generated vs. Real Images” and attributing images to their sources into a single framework. This is achieved by including real images in our dataset and treating them as an additional ‘generator’, enabling a more detailed analysis of AI-generated content. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n短期依存性を有する多モード深偽物検出のための自己監督型双方向同期推定〖JST機械翻訳〗 | 文献情報 | J-GLOBAL 科学技術総合リンクセンター (https://jglobal.jst.go.jp/detail?JGLOBAL_ID=202602288434469975)\nciteturn3search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Self-supervised Bidirectional Synchronization Estimation for Multimodal Deepfake Detection with Short-term Dependency ... Xiao Man ... (National Key Laboratory of Parallel and Distributed Computing, College of Computer Science and Technology, National University of Defense Technology, Changsha, China)\n\n文献\n\nJ-GLOBAL ID：202602288434469975   整理番号：26A0169595\n\n# 短期依存性を有する多モード深偽物検出のための自己監督型双方向同期推定〖JST機械翻訳〗\n\nSelf-supervised Bidirectional Synchronization Estimation for Multimodal Deepfake Detection